@startuml
title SplitSmart expense review and final ledger posting
actor Reviewer
participant "Review client" as Client
participant "ReviewExpense use case" as App
participant "Authorization / state rules" as Domain
database "Transaction / repositories" as Store
participant "Projection updater" as Projection
queue "Notification outbox" as Outbox

Reviewer -> Client : approve or reject
Client -> App : decide(expenseId, action, expectedVersion, requestId)
App -> Domain : authorize reviewer; validate pending state/version
alt unauthorized
  Domain --> App : forbidden
  App --> Client : reject; no state or ledger change
else stale, already final, or duplicate conflict
  Domain --> App : conflict or idempotent prior result
  App --> Client : explicit current result; no duplicate posting
else authorized and current
  App -> Store : begin transaction; append immutable decision
  alt reject
    App -> Store : set REJECTED; create no obligations
    Store --> App : commit
    App --> Client : rejected; no balance effect
  else approve, more stages remain
    App -> Store : advance stage; keep PENDING_REVIEW
    Store --> App : commit
    App --> Client : awaiting next reviewer; no balance effect
  else final approval
    App -> Domain : derive one obligation per positive non-payer share
    Domain --> App : distinct obligations with obligationId\nand (expense, debtor, creditor, kind) key
    App -> Store : conditional final-state transition; insert all obligations
    App -> Store : enforce unique source keys; update projection or mark dirty
    App -> Store : enqueue notification intents in transaction
    alt duplicate source / transaction failure
      Store --> App : rollback or idempotent existing result
      App --> Client : no partial posting; report conflict/failure
    else committed once
      Store --> App : approved + all obligation postings
      App -> Outbox : dispatch committed intents asynchronously
      App --> Client : approved; canonical balance result
    end
  end
end
note over Store
Approval decision, final state and every obligation commit atomically.
Pending/rejected expenses have no ledger obligations.
Projection is rebuildable and never the source of truth.
end note
@enduml
